# Generated diagrams are derived files, not sources. `homelab/spec/*.json` is
# the source; these are what archify renders from it.
#
# -merge tells git never to attempt a textual three-way merge on them. A
# line-level merge of two 700KB rendered documents does not produce a valid
# page, it produces a broken one that still looks like HTML — the worst kind of
# conflict resolution, because it can pass review.
#
# The correct resolution is always the same and never involves reading the
# conflict: settle the spec, then regenerate. Nothing is lost, because nothing
# in these files exists anywhere but in the spec.
#
# -diff keeps them out of diffs and `git log -p`, where a re-render shows as
# thousands of changed lines that mean nothing.
homelab/topology/index.html      -merge -diff
homelab/changes/**/index.html    -merge -diff
homelab/changes/**/*.receipt.json -diff
